entries.text:
As an additional downtime move, you may choose to forage for ingredients that can be used in potioncraft. Roll a d4 and add your Instinct. You collect a number of ingredients equal to the result of this roll. For each collected ingredient, roll a d6 to determine its properties when used in a potion. Work with the GM to describe these ingredients and add them to your inventory.

1. Heal: Clear 2 Hit Points (2d8 direct physical damage if inverted);
2. Soothe: Clear 2 Stress;
3. Empower: You gain a +2 bonus to your next damage roll;
4. Enhance: You gain a +1 bonus to your next action or reaction roll
5. Bolster: Double the effectiveness of all ingredients in the potion;
6. Invert: All ingredient effects become harmful (Mark a Stress or Hit Point instead of clearing it, receive a -1 penalty to the next Roll instead of a +1 bonus, etc.);

When you take the “Work on a Project” downtime move, you may create a potion using gathered ingredients. The number of ingredients you can include in a potion equals your Proficiency, and the project’s Countdown duration is equal to the number of included ingredients. The difficulty is 10 + the number of ingredients.

By default, a potion must be ingested to take effect. However, you may alter the potion for it to activate on contact or disperse as a gas and affect all creatures within Close range of the impact point. If you do so, double the project’s Countdown.
